{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QonSU12HYDfi5zoS38VNgC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# lib/loops/harden.sh — the harden loop adapter.\n3\t#\n4\t# One file owns everything the engine needs to know about how to launch and\n5\t# control the harden loop. Auto-discovered by lib/loops.sh from lib/loops/*.sh.\n6\t#\n7\t# Contract (called as almanac_loop_harden_<verb>):\n8\t#   exec_argv   — launch: populate _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV with the runner exec tokens\n9\t#                 for a given target/rounds. harden's runner is the convergence\n10\t#                 loop reached via `almanac harden <target> --loop`.\n11\t#\n12\t# Control contract (signal_file) inherits the default `.harden-stop` /\n13\t# `.harden-steer` convention from lib/loops.sh — no adapter override needed.\n14\t\n15\t# Build harden's runner exec command into _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV (the launcher execs\n16\t# it). harden has no standalone runner script — its convergence loop runs through\n17\t# the CLI (`almanac harden <target> --loop [--rounds N]`), so the adapter yields\n18\t# that bin/almanac invocation. The reviewer/role config rides on environment\n19\t# exported by the launcher, not argv. Requires $ALMANAC_HOME (set by every entry\n20\t# point).\n21\talmanac_loop_harden_exec_argv() {\n22\t  local target=\"$1\" rounds=\"${2:-}\"\n23\t  _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV=(bash \"$ALMANAC_HOME/bin/almanac\" harden \"$target\" --loop)\n24\t  [ -n \"$rounds\" ] && _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV+=(--rounds \"$rounds\")\n25\t  return 0\n26\t}\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a891a69f-75d4-4053-b662-17c3d63f7902","uuid":"65379b14-489c-4097-9295-5466a4bb358a","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:38:59.305Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/lib/loops/harden.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# lib/loops/harden.sh — the harden loop adapter.\n#\n# One file owns everything the engine needs to know about how to launch and\n# control the harden loop. Auto-discovered by lib/loops.sh from lib/loops/*.sh.\n#\n# Contract (called as almanac_loop_harden_<verb>):\n#   exec_argv   — launch: populate _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV with the runner exec tokens\n#                 for a given target/rounds. harden's runner is the convergence\n#                 loop reached via `almanac harden <target> --loop`.\n#\n# Control contract (signal_file) inherits the default `.harden-stop` /\n# `.harden-steer` convention from lib/loops.sh — no adapter override needed.\n\n# Build harden's runner exec command into _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV (the launcher execs\n# it). harden has no standalone runner script — its convergence loop runs through\n# the CLI (`almanac harden <target> --loop [--rounds N]`), so the adapter yields\n# that bin/almanac invocation. The reviewer/role config rides on environment\n# exported by the launcher, not argv. Requires $ALMANAC_HOME (set by every entry\n# point).\nalmanac_loop_harden_exec_argv() {\n  local target=\"$1\" rounds=\"${2:-}\"\n  _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV=(bash \"$ALMANAC_HOME/bin/almanac\" harden \"$target\" --loop)\n  [ -n \"$rounds\" ] && _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV+=(--rounds \"$rounds\")\n  return 0\n}\n","numLines":27,"startLine":1,"totalLines":27}}}
