{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UHdJ9NLTdaNwsKjmjsruFi","type":"tool_result","content":"36\t\n37\t## Roles & lenses\n38\t\n39\t- **Role** — a configurable slot that resolves to (provider, model, effort): ralph's `agent`; harden's `conductor` / `reviewer` / `fixer`. Resolution layers lens → role → consumer-wide → default.\n40\t- **Lens** — a harden reviewer perspective (correctness, security, perf, edge/tests, contracts). Reviewers fan out one per lens and may mix providers.\n41\t\n42\t## Seams (gum-or-plain)\n43\t\n44\t- **UI seam** — `almanac_loop_ui_*` (choose/input/confirm/render): gum when a controlling terminal is present, plain numbered fallback otherwise. Lives in `lib/ui.sh`.\n45\t\n46\t## Module map (`lib/`)\n47\t\n48\tThe engine is split into cohesive modules — each file's interface is its test surface; `loop-core.sh` (the old 1619-line god-module) is **deleted**, not kept as a barrel. **Callers source only the modules they use** (explicit dependencies — no implicit \"source the whole engine\"). Skill entry points (`once.sh`/`afk.sh`/`prompt.sh`) bootstrap `ALMANAC_HOME`, then source their specific modules.\n49\t\n50\t| file | owns |\n51\t|------|------|\n52\t| `lib/core.sh` | CLI helpers (`_die`/`_info`/…) + `ALMANAC_HOME` resolve |\n53\t| `lib/ui.sh` | gum-or-plain UI seam |\n54\t| `lib/role.sh` | role → (provider, model, effort) resolution |\n55\t| `lib/agent.sh` | `agent_capture`/`agent_stream`/`agent_raw` + provider dispatch |\n56\t| `lib/providers/<name>.sh` | provider adapters (auto-discovered) |\n57\t| `lib/loops.sh` | loop-adapter discovery + dispatch |\n58\t| `lib/loops/<name>.sh` | loop adapters (auto-discovered) |\n59\t| `lib/feedback.sh` | feedback detection + runner |\n60\t| `lib/run.sh` | run registry + run-status record + generic TSV record engine + control (stop/steer/watch) + worker health + hub read-views |\n61\t| `lib/worker.sh` | worker orchestration (background fan-out) + worker-status record schema (uses run.sh's engine) |\n62\t| `lib/loop-launcher.sh` | the launcher |\n63\t| `lib/harden-core.sh` | harden loop (declares its real deps) |\n64\t| `lib/converge-core.sh` | converge loop (declares its real deps) |\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a891a69f-75d4-4053-b662-17c3d63f7902","uuid":"c61c1c5f-110d-4df6-bb96-7f9f2665d45b","timestamp":"2026-05-26T14:49:42.120Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/CONTEXT.md","content":"\n## Roles & lenses\n\n- **Role** — a configurable slot that resolves to (provider, model, effort): ralph's `agent`; harden's `conductor` / `reviewer` / `fixer`. Resolution layers lens → role → consumer-wide → default.\n- **Lens** — a harden reviewer perspective (correctness, security, perf, edge/tests, contracts). Reviewers fan out one per lens and may mix providers.\n\n## Seams (gum-or-plain)\n\n- **UI seam** — `almanac_loop_ui_*` (choose/input/confirm/render): gum when a controlling terminal is present, plain numbered fallback otherwise. Lives in `lib/ui.sh`.\n\n## Module map (`lib/`)\n\nThe engine is split into cohesive modules — each file's interface is its test surface; `loop-core.sh` (the old 1619-line god-module) is **deleted**, not kept as a barrel. **Callers source only the modules they use** (explicit dependencies — no implicit \"source the whole engine\"). Skill entry points (`once.sh`/`afk.sh`/`prompt.sh`) bootstrap `ALMANAC_HOME`, then source their specific modules.\n\n| file | owns |\n|------|------|\n| `lib/core.sh` | CLI helpers (`_die`/`_info`/…) + `ALMANAC_HOME` resolve |\n| `lib/ui.sh` | gum-or-plain UI seam |\n| `lib/role.sh` | role → (provider, model, effort) resolution |\n| `lib/agent.sh` | `agent_capture`/`agent_stream`/`agent_raw` + provider dispatch |\n| `lib/providers/<name>.sh` | provider adapters (auto-discovered) |\n| `lib/loops.sh` | loop-adapter discovery + dispatch |\n| `lib/loops/<name>.sh` | loop adapters (auto-discovered) |\n| `lib/feedback.sh` | feedback detection + runner |\n| `lib/run.sh` | run registry + run-status record + generic TSV record engine + control (stop/steer/watch) + worker health + hub read-views |\n| `lib/worker.sh` | worker orchestration (background fan-out) + worker-status record schema (uses run.sh's engine) |\n| `lib/loop-launcher.sh` | the launcher |\n| `lib/harden-core.sh` | harden loop (declares its real deps) |\n| `lib/converge-core.sh` | converge loop (declares its real deps) |\n","numLines":30,"startLine":36,"totalLines":65}}}
